{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q7339208","formula":"C₁₅H₁₆ClFN₂O₄","hill":"C15H16ClFN2O4","elements":["H","C","N","O","F","Cl"],"composition":{"C":15.0,"F":1.0,"H":16.0,"N":2.0,"O":4.0,"Cl":1.0},"names":{"en":"Ro60-0175"},"descriptions":{"en":"Ro60-0175, or Ro-600175, also known as (S)-5-fluoro-6-chloro-α-methylisotryptamine ((S)-5-F-6-Cl-isoAMT), is a serotonin 5-HT2 receptor agonist of the isotryptamine family developed by Hoffmann–La Roche, which has applications in scientific research. It is the enantiopure (S)- isomer of the 5-fluoro and 6-chloro derivative of α-methylisotryptamine (isoAMT). It acts as a potent and selective agonist of both the serotonin 5-HT2B and 5-HT2C receptor subtypes, with good selectivity over the closely related serotonin 5-HT2A subtype, and little or no affinity at other receptors."},"fame":5,"pubchemCid":6446435,"mass":342.75,"charge":0,"smiles":"C[C@@H](CN1C=CC2=CC(=C(C=C21)Cl)F)N.C(=C/C(=O)O)\\C(=O)O","inchikey":"CEPHEXXZGQBXGT-XZTIXWOLSA-N","iupac":"(E)-but-2-enedioic acid;(2S)-1-(6-chloro-5-fluoroindol-1-yl)propan-2-amine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"6446435","atoms":39,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-3.3,"y":1.357,"z":1.438,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.944,"y":1.559,"z":0.764,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.288,"y":0.195,"z":0.475,"el":"C"},{"x":0.108,"y":0.305,"z":0.072,"el":"N"},{"x":0.542,"y":0.252,"z":-1.228,"el":"C"},{"x":1.911,"y":0.382,"z":-1.226,"el":"C"},{"x":2.332,"y":0.509,"z":0.125,"el":"C"},{"x":3.59,"y":0.664,"z":0.738,"el":"C"},{"x":3.659,"y":0.758,"z":2.129,"el":"C"},{"x":2.511,"y":0.7,"z":2.913,"el":"C"},{"x":1.251,"y":0.546,"z":2.327,"el":"C"},{"x":1.185,"y":0.453,"z":0.926,"el":"C"},{"x":2.621,"y":0.82,"z":4.629,"el":"Cl"},{"x":4.865,"y":0.907,"z":2.697,"el":"F"},{"x":-2.148,"y":2.347,"z":-0.4